WEBVTT

00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:28.800
Always sought defense against a common enemy by uniting their resources and ingenuity.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:35.130
In the very earliest times, the concept of a civil defense was deeply rooted in the anxieties

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:37.750
of the community over the terrors of the day.

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:44.400
Walls around the cities of old were attempts to safeguard the civilian population from

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:45.440
enemy onslaught.

00:00:47.270 --> 00:00:52.300
To inhabitants of the medieval community, the catapult and the ballista were terrifying

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:56.880
weapons and the only possible defense against them was stronger and higher walls.

00:00:58.980 --> 00:00:59.960
in our own planet.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.600
civilian communities developed within the protecting walls of the stockade.

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:14.140
Today, no barricade is high enough or strong enough

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:16.940
to protect us from a possible onslaught of weapons

00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:20.210
that dwarf any in history and their destructive potential.

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:23.060
To reduce the effectiveness of these weapons,

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:26.000
should they ever be used in enemy attack on our nation,

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:29.960
a civil defense effort that challenges our ingenuity and resources...

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:36.320
is necessary. In the United States, responsibility for civil defense planning

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:44.520
at the federal level is lodged within the Department of Defense. The development

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:50.780
of civil defense programs is a joint responsibility shared by the federal, state,

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:56.420
and local governments. This film will consider civil defense on the local government level.

00:02:01.630 --> 00:02:15.260
Hometown USA, a church, a school, a factory, an office building.

00:02:17.730 --> 00:02:22.510
Today, these and other structures bear a marking on which the survival of our country might well depend.

00:02:26.740 --> 00:02:29.980
Shelter, protection from dangerous radioactive fallout.

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:32.260
the inevitable result of nuclear warfare.

00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:35.130
To provide enough shelter space for the community

00:02:35.130 --> 00:02:39.050
is the first and foremost consideration of local civil defense planning.

00:02:42.790 --> 00:02:45.690
The National Fallout Shelter Program has as its goal

00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:50.220
a shelter space for every man, woman, and child in the United States.

00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:53.240
In cities and towns throughout the country,

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:57.340
public shelters have been surveyed, marked, and provisioned

00:02:57.780 --> 00:02:59.940
in a continuous program of shelter...

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:07.700
expansion. With availability of shelter protection for its citizens, the prime local civil defense

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:13.200
responsibility is that each municipality or rural district must organize its local

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:19.380
existing government agencies for emergency operations to meet the threat of enemy attack

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:27.800
or natural disaster. This is the objective of civil defense planning. Over the nation,

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:29.980
local government officials meet...

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:34.990
periodically to discuss civil defense emergency measures. The chief executive or governing

00:03:34.990 --> 00:03:40.700
body of the locality is responsible for civil defense protection for that community. Appointed

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:45.330
by the mayor or appropriate town or county officials, the civil defense director acts

00:03:45.330 --> 00:03:54.810
as staff man, coordinating the various emergency activities. The logistics of survival are

00:03:54.810 --> 00:03:59.860
complex and varied. They depend on technological knowledge, which has developed at an incredible

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:09.110
pace, spurred on by the unique dangers of our time. Survival materials and equipment are researched,

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:20.790
engineered, and fabricated. However, craftsmanship alone will not do the civil defense job. This can

00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:26.160
only be accomplished by firmly organized emergency skills and an awareness by each

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:29.920
local government official of what his department can do to meet.

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:38.050
civil defense need. Let's hear first from our chief of police, Mr. Condon. Harry. The police

00:04:38.050 --> 00:04:44.160
function in civil defense is a natural expansion of our routine assignment of protection and keeping

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:50.810
law in order. In our headquarters, existing facilities for police purposes can be quickly

00:04:50.810 --> 00:04:57.560
and effectively put to use in a national emergency or natural disaster type situation. Our siren

00:04:57.560 --> 00:04:59.960
warning system would function in emergency situations.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:11.210
Communication facilities linking police headquarters to key points in the community will be used in civil defense planning and operation.

00:05:15.420 --> 00:05:23.040
The handling of crowds, national emergency would add a considerable burden, particularly in the critical movement to shelter period.

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:29.760
This would be a police responsibility and we carry on training and planning programs to meet civil defense needs.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:40.260
Mr. Mayor, in the sanitation department, our emergency assignment might include helping with decontamination.

00:05:42.350 --> 00:05:47.970
Contamination is caused by radioactive fallout material settling after a nuclear explosion.

00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:57.390
Decontamination of buildings and streets and equipment might be necessary before an area could be used for its intended purpose.

00:05:58.420 --> 00:05:59.600
Much radioactive fallout...

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:06.150
can be removed methods include hosing down the area with water or sweeping

00:06:06.150 --> 00:06:15.010
gentlemen essential to the disaster situation whether natural or man-made

00:06:15.010 --> 00:06:20.920
is a rescue capability often the responsibility of the fire department in

00:06:20.920 --> 00:06:24.640
any large-scale emergency we would have to face the fact that numbers of people

00:06:24.640 --> 00:06:29.260
might be trapped in wreckage in this town we have our own rescue vehicle

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:35.800
to handle a variety of disaster situations the town paid for part of the cost of the vehicle and

00:06:35.800 --> 00:06:40.230
the federal government contributed the rest as part of its program of providing funds for certain

00:06:40.230 --> 00:06:52.310
approved civil defense equipment thank you chief public works mr mayor our public works department

00:06:52.310 --> 00:06:57.470
has the emergency assignment of keeping the town's facilities operating as normally as possible

00:06:58.200 --> 00:06:59.980
Among other functions, we work with the time.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:04.410
engineering personnel and the utility companies in developing plans for

00:07:04.410 --> 00:07:09.230
standby services if they should become necessary. Public works trucks used in

00:07:09.230 --> 00:07:12.720
road maintenance and for other purposes might be called into service for

00:07:12.720 --> 00:07:19.720
emergency transportation needs. Thank you and now gentlemen our information

00:07:19.720 --> 00:07:26.320
office. Public information is a vital element in civil defense operations. Now

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:29.900
in time of emergency people have a great need

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:35.170
to know what is happening. Now my job is to see that the public is provided with

00:07:35.170 --> 00:07:41.190
survival information through every possible channel of communication. As

00:07:41.190 --> 00:07:44.370
your civil defense director I must stress the importance of being fully

00:07:44.370 --> 00:07:49.820
efficient in times of emergency. First, a shelter must be manned by efficient

00:07:49.820 --> 00:07:55.490
personnel who can provide leadership within the shelter. One of our shelter

00:07:55.490 --> 00:07:59.770
manager instructors has just come back from taking a course at a federal civil

00:07:59.770 --> 00:07:59.970
the

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:05.320
He's going to set up a training program here in town for shelter managers.

00:08:07.550 --> 00:08:16.860
Shelters should be adequately stocked with food, water, radiological, medical, and sanitation equipment.

00:08:17.950 --> 00:08:21.950
Federal government provides the survival support for licensed shelters.

00:08:23.430 --> 00:08:29.470
But it's up to us in local government to come up with any additional items such as cots,

00:08:30.220 --> 00:08:35.000
chairs, or blankets, special foods, and medication.

00:08:37.360 --> 00:08:39.120
Gentlemen, an item of vital concern.

00:08:39.920 --> 00:08:42.220
All of our local government civil defense activities

00:08:42.220 --> 00:08:45.070
may be conditioned by the radiological situation.

00:08:46.020 --> 00:08:47.580
Like the fallout shelter program itself,

00:08:47.720 --> 00:08:50.010
the radiological defense program is a product

00:08:50.010 --> 00:08:51.010
of the nuclear age.

00:08:52.030 --> 00:08:53.630
Now, our function in the time of enemy attack

00:08:53.630 --> 00:08:57.190
would be analysis and evaluation of the fallout radiation

00:08:57.190 --> 00:08:59.970
data and the providing technical guidance.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:05.570
in this area. Many of the people assigned to emergency tasks, such as firemen and

00:09:05.570 --> 00:09:10.930
policemen, are also trained in radiological monitoring. Our training

00:09:10.930 --> 00:09:15.310
situation gives us experience with sample radiological materials in control

00:09:15.310 --> 00:09:22.910
exercises. In all of our emergency operations, the big need is for trained

00:09:22.910 --> 00:09:29.490
personnel, but most important of all, we need qualified instructors. The Civil

00:09:29.490 --> 00:09:29.790
Defense

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:35.690
operated by the federal government, provide a means of instructor training and each municipality

00:09:35.690 --> 00:09:40.780
or rural community should see to it that training courses are set up in such vital

00:09:40.780 --> 00:09:46.130
civil defense subjects as shelter management, planning and operations, and radiological

00:09:46.130 --> 00:09:57.060
monitoring. A meeting of skills and capabilities, plans for a pool of manpower and equipment with

00:09:57.060 --> 00:09:59.930
one goal, emergency protection for members of...

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:05.580
family, for friends, for neighbors. Other talents and skills too will be brought

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:09.460
into the civil defense picture by an enterprising local government. The

00:10:09.460 --> 00:10:14.030
clergyman, the welfare worker, the administrator, the merchant, all can

00:10:14.030 --> 00:10:25.040
assist in the emergency preparation. The heart of local civil defense operation

00:10:25.040 --> 00:10:29.740
is an emergency operating center which must coordinate emergency activities

00:10:29.740 --> 00:10:29.980
from

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:35.460
a protected area. This town is one of many in the United States which is developing an effective

00:10:35.460 --> 00:10:41.040
civil defense program. Its emergency operating center is located in the basement of the municipal

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:49.960
building. In time of disaster, the emergency operating center will be staffed with personnel

00:10:49.960 --> 00:10:52.640
assigned to the various civil defence functions.

00:11:00.120 --> 00:11:06.520
Information as to conditions outside would be received here and plotted on a map of the area

00:11:06.580 --> 00:11:09.860
indicating the disposition of the town's existing resources.

00:11:11.860 --> 00:11:17.460
From this chart, the Civil Defense Director could tell at a glance what must be committed to any particular area.

00:11:18.130 --> 00:11:26.000
Markers are coded to designate fire, police, ambulance, rescue, or other resources required in the distress area.

00:11:39.470 --> 00:11:43.670
At the administration desk, the Civil Defense Director takes charge of the activities.

00:11:47.500 --> 00:11:51.640
Vital to the Emergency Operating Center is a communications capability

00:11:51.640 --> 00:11:56.970
that links the center with key municipal facilities, radio stations, and county officials.

00:12:00.480 --> 00:12:05.180
Radio and telephone provide a network for the exchange of important emergency data.

00:12:07.880 --> 00:12:12.660
A potential source of communications for civil defense emergency is amateur radioactivity.

00:12:13.050 --> 00:12:18.810
In many communities, HAM operators are licensed to tie in their facilities with a civil defense network.

00:12:19.820 --> 00:12:22.220
Communications apparatus is tested periodically,

00:12:22.950 --> 00:12:27.590
with each municipality usually reporting to county or state control centers.

00:12:27.590 --> 00:12:29.960
A ready communications...

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:43.060
capability is invaluable in the disaster situation. When conditions permit, a mobile communications

00:12:43.060 --> 00:12:53.900
van may be used as a control center. Civil defense planning calls for an augmented communications

00:12:53.900 --> 00:12:57.130
network equipped to cope with a variety of critical needs.

00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:29.040
Supplementing the work of existing local government which has inherent responsibility in emergency may be the Red Cross, traditionally serving in disaster situations, may also be available from military personnel in the local community, wherever this would not interfere with the primary armed forces mission.

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:41.340
Local business and industry are essential in providing the required shelter space.

00:13:42.260 --> 00:13:46.680
Federal government surveys approve portions of thousands of buildings throughout the nation

00:13:46.700 --> 00:13:48.020
as fallout shelters.

00:13:48.830 --> 00:13:53.610
Each building must be licensed with the owner's signature, indicating his approval for its

00:13:53.610 --> 00:13:54.870
use as a public shelter.

00:13:55.710 --> 00:13:58.750
This is the responsibility of local government.

00:14:01.370 --> 00:14:07.490
The shelter markings on the buildings in our cities and towns are symbols of an ever-expanding civil defense effort.

00:14:10.430 --> 00:14:18.880
Its success, perhaps the survival of our nation, will depend on how well each community organizes for and meets its emergency responsibilities.

00:14:22.830 --> 00:14:29.980
No one can predict whether this nation will ever be the victim of enemy attack, nor do we know...

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:32.200
when or where natural disaster may strike.

00:14:32.900 --> 00:14:34.360
If and when these should occur,

00:14:34.950 --> 00:14:36.370
we must be ready to meet them.

00:14:37.670 --> 00:14:40.210
We will be ready only if the full potential

00:14:40.210 --> 00:14:43.000
of civil defense is understood and acted upon

00:14:43.000 --> 00:14:44.900
by the federal and state governments,

00:14:45.290 --> 00:14:47.010
and especially by local government

00:14:47.010 --> 00:14:50.060
and all persons charged with community responsibility.

00:14:50.810 --> 00:14:53.390
Local government can and must meet the challenge

00:14:53.390 --> 00:14:54.410
of the nuclear age.

00:14:55.890 --> 00:14:57.750
Communities all over the United States

00:14:57.750 --> 00:14:59.980
share a common problem and a common problem.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:04.740
responsibility to develop within their existing local governments an expanded

00:15:04.740 --> 00:15:09.160
capability for the protection of their citizens in time of emergency.
